EVALUATION.md §1, DECISIONS 331: why a type is broken is not traced. `Box`, whose check names a
broken value, warns for `box`; `Holder`, whose check names the broken type Gem, warns for
`holder`; Gem, which no value's type reaches, reports nothing.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Broken value.
let limit: Int = "ten"

/// Box.
record Box {
  /// N.
  n: Int

  check fits: n < limit else "big"
}

/// Gem.
record Gem {
  /// W.
  w: Int = "heavy"
}

/// Holder.
record Holder {
  /// N.
  n: Int

  check gems: Gem { w: n } == Gem { w: n } else "never"
}

/// Typed by Box.
let box: Box = { n: 1 }

/// Typed by Holder.
let holder: Holder = { n: 1 }
-- findings.txt --
error[E3002]  a/a.canon:5:18
  expected Int, found String

warning[W4001]  a/a.canon:8:8
  1 value was not evaluated or checked because a.Box is broken: fix the errors in it or in the types it names

error[E3002]  a/a.canon:18:12
  expected Int, found String

warning[W4001]  a/a.canon:22:8
  1 value was not evaluated or checked because a.Holder is broken: fix the errors in it or in the types it names

2 errors, 2 warnings in 1 package (…)
